  body: |
    # Self-employed earnings assessment period for ESA

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source uses gross receipts and paid expenses during an earnings assessment period and varies period selection for a new business or changed trading pattern.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 50051 expressly says this period must not be confused with the ESA assessment phase. Newer, established and changed businesses have different provisions; the period is not automatically the preceding tax year or thirteen weeks.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 50051, PDF page 12](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/61976ff0d3bf7f055fce727f/dmgch50.pdf#page=12)
    - [DMG 50052, PDF page 12](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/61976ff0d3bf7f055fce727f/dmgch50.pdf#page=12)
    - [DMG 50054, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/61976ff0d3bf7f055fce727f/dmgch50.pdf#page=13)
    - [DMG 50060, PDF page 13](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/61976ff0d3bf7f055fce727f/dmgch50.pdf#page=13)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:30.643995Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication, revision or commencement date. Source-stated dates retain their own role and precision.

